/-!
# Component control in the A₅ centralizer argument

The first assertion of 13.6.16 is proved from the explicit genuine earlier
inputs, retaining the universal A₅ choice condition and the actual Sylow,
component, quotient and normalizer conventions. The characteristic-subgroup
contradiction is also proved with C characteristic inside T_v and mapped to G.

The radical-supplement replacement needed for assertion (2), and the
Frattini/Thompson argument giving assertion (3), remain to be assembled.
No complete three-part version of 13.6.16 is asserted by this module yet.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined 1 March 2004 manuscript, printed p.930.
-/
